name: sim.insertObjectIntoPointCloud
description: Inserts an object into a point cloud, as points
luaSynopsis: int totalPointCnt = sim.insertObjectIntoPointCloud(int pointCloudHandle, int objectHandle, int options, float gridSize, list color = None, float duplicateTolerance = None)
pythonSynopsis: int totalPointCnt = sim.insertObjectIntoPointCloud(int pointCloudHandle, int objectHandle, int options, float gridSize, int[] color = nil, float duplicateTolerance = nil)
inputs:
1. pointCloudHandle: handle of the point cloud
2. objectHandle: handle of the object to insert. Only potentially collidable objects are supported
3. options: reserved. Set to 0
4. gridSize: when a shape is inserted, it will first be converted to an OC tree with a given grid or voxel size
5. color: array containing an RGB triplet, specifying the red, green and blue color components (0 - 255). Can be None/nil.
6. duplicateTolerance: a minimum distance tolerance value that is used to avoid duplicate points
outputs:
1. totalPointCnt: the total number of points in the point cloud
replacedBy:
- name: addFromObjects, class: pointCloud, file: pointCloud_addFromObjects.method
